            },
            {
              "$type": "Models.Core.Folder, Models",
              "ShowInDocs": true,
              "Name": "BFG",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                  "Text": "These data are for an experiment with fertilizer, irrigation and fertigation treatments established in a 10-year-old _P. radiata_ plantation near Canberra, Australia. The experiment was officially entitled Biology of Forest Growth (BFG) as if focused on improving the physiogical understanding of  growth of this species in a somewhat common Australian environment. \r\n\nNumerous publications about this experiment reported on its management, tree growth, biomass components, phenology, climate, and soils. Many of these publications were produced in a special issue of Forest Ecology and Management (Volume 52, Issues 1–4, September 1992) several from which data have been sourced for developing the APSIM Pimus model: [#benson1992biology], [#benson1992dynamics], [#crane1992accumulation], [#cremer1992relations], [#khanna1992effects], [#kirschbaum1999cenw], [#mcmurtrie1992using], [#myers1992site], [#raison1992biology], [#raison1992dynamicsI], [#raison1992dynamicsII], [#raison1990effects], and [#snowdon1992effects]. A later thesis [#pongracic2001influence] and paper [#waterworth2007effects] also provided data. Many of these data and addition data were also provided by Keryn Paul (CSIRO), which we greatly apprecaited.\n\n",
                  "Name": "Memo",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [],
                  "Enabled": true,
                  "ReadOnly": false
                },
                {
