                          "Comments": "Loamy Sand - Soil water properties (BD, CLL, DUL, SAT, AIRDRY) of this soil are based on a generic soil developed as part of Liddicoat C, Hayman P, et al. (2012) Climate change, wheat production and erosion risk in South Australia’s cropping zone: Linking crop simulation modelling to soil landscape mapping, Government of South Australia, through Department of Environment, Water and Natural Resources. http://www.environment.sa.gov.au/files/sharedassets/public/science/soil_and_land/kb-gen-climate-change-wheat-production-and-erosion-risk.pdf (Section 3.3 and Appendix F). These were developed for use with wheat with some level of verification of yield predictions (see report for details).  Other APSIM soil parameters were based on ‘A protocol for the development of soil parameter values for use in APSIM’ by Dalgliesh et al. OC% was estimated based on soil texture and pH set at 7.0. No soil chemical values were estimated. Soil chemical properties may need to be adapted to reflect local conditions and subsoil constraints.",
