        {
          "$type": "Models.Core.Folder, Models",
          "ShowInDocs": true,
          "Name": "Reponse to N Fertilizer",
          "ResourceName": null,
          "Children": [
            {
              "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
              "Text": "Pinus response to rate of N fertiliser are often asymptotic, the plateau of which is determined by other limiting factors. In the sensibility test presented here, an infertile soil at Stockdale, Victoria, Australia, was used as the basis for the simulations _P. radiata_ was fertilised at 3 years of age and stem volume assessed at 26 years of age.  \r\n\nOperationally, _P. radiata_ plantations in Australia receive several hundered kg N/ha during a rotation. The approximate optimum rate simulated (90% of maximum) was 900 kg N/ha, which is therefore within the range of expectation.\r\n\r\n",
              "Name": "Memo",
              "ResourceName": null,
              "Children": [],
              "Enabled": true,
              "ReadOnly": false
            },
            {
              "$type": "Models.Factorial.Experiment, Models",
